# Kanban inquiry cards

When a feature file has frontmatter `labels` including **`inquiry`** (case-insensitive), follow [kanban-markdown/SKILL.md](../skills/kanban-markdown/SKILL.md) § Inquiry cards.

## User provides

- `## Description` (required)
- `## Feature Areas` (optional — omit when not about an existing product area)

## Agent provides

- `## Response` — answer the question; include content usable to create follow-up feature/bug cards later
- `## Label Paths` — when user provided **Feature Areas**, resolve via `docs/feature-areas.yaml`

## Workflow

1. Confirm **Description** present
2. Resolve **Feature Areas** → **Label Paths** when areas are set
3. `todo` → `in-progress` → research (read-only)
4. Write **Response** on the card → `review`
5. User may spawn new cards from **Suggested follow-up cards** in Response

## Do not

- Use **Decisions**, **Corrective Action**, or **Acceptance Criteria** on inquiry cards
- Implement code unless the user explicitly asks on the same card
- Require pytest before **Review** (no code changes by default)

## Full workflow

See `.cursor/skills/kanban-markdown/SKILL.md` for lifecycle and **Response** content guidelines.
